{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:40Z","created_by_operation":"op_df82d93b9d78477fb22075a6516db635","id":"pg_26fbeb04408f536b96e4e1c5b4d14b59","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langchain-ai-openwiki-development-md-e92cc11723a8-e1c5b4d14b59.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_76ea5aeb7ffa597ab94514702df87eca"],"title":"langchain-ai/openwiki/DEVELOPMENT.md @ e92cc11723a8","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:40Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df82d93b9d78477fb22075a6516db635"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:40Z","created_by_operation":"op_df82d93b9d78477fb22075a6516db635","id":"pg_58e6da11887153a8a4b267b0dd7bea89","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langchain-ai-openwiki-agents-md-e92cc11723a8-67b0dd7bea89.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a879c3adffc15df39c8fa562bca108d0"],"title":"langchain-ai/openwiki/AGENTS.md @ e92cc11723a8","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:40Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df82d93b9d78477fb22075a6516db635"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_148cfc859248fea87666537a7e52ff3d943e379730ff796e1e91d4e2d0ca04af"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Thirteen model providers are supported out of the box, including OpenAI (default, gpt-5.6-terra), Anthropic, Gemini, Bedrock, Copilot, OpenRouter, and any OpenAI-compatible endpoint via base URL and key."},{"claim_ids":["clm_23d70d663bfdbfde2118e42a646d7cf5074e77fae68ab7ba849e2986f108f797"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Coding-agent integrations expose an MCP page-job lifecycle via tools named openwiki_begin, openwiki_submit_plan, openwiki_next_page, openwiki_inspect_page_claims, openwiki_submit_page, and openwiki_finish for Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, and Cursor."},{"claim_ids":["clm_297282fa7f053d3a0a473513e571555c644e12b07fdcee8445db50113c17dd37"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Personal mode supports nine connectors (Custom MCP, Notion, Slack, Gmail, X, Web Search, Hacker News, LangSmith, local git); connector secrets are referenced by env var in ~/.openwiki/.env and never stored in config files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2b778e362b789acf06c003e9b25f5e597765d6c63ab65aca0828a993832ae22f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"OpenWiki is a CLI that writes and maintains a wiki for a codebase or personal knowledge, generating linked Markdown intended as agent memory, with an interactive visualizer for humans."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4192d1f20a41790de62927a8bf4e23e50a578911d424b6b5c161ae53da67143e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool offers two modes: a default 'code' wiki for the current repository written to openwiki/, and a 'personal' wiki for connected sources written to ~/.openwiki/wiki."},{"claim_ids":["clm_458eb8c35b488e7bbd5daeb0ea605e97f9f53dbdf6a981e784eea8dd052280f2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Local state (credentials, personal wiki, connector data, history, skills) lives under ~/.openwiki by default, relocatable via OPENWIKI_CONFIG_DIR; the override does not move or delete the existing directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_528cc5c643665c905dd3e157be0e367b6ab38dfc352531c99cbc5402e53ff779"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors adding another coding-agent integration are directed to follow the 'Adding a coding-agent integration' section of CONTRIBUTING.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9433e3f7348319bb6dce728194df4e95348727219e5bf8067ffa98bf1cdf21cc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Grounded Claims track material propositions in code wikis back to versioned repository evidence (e.g. repo:// paths with line ranges), stored as sidecars under openwiki/.claims/ rather than in the Markdown."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a27e5781554a893e3a776cb10305633de0a19df1691c8c5eebb56741792b23e2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository generation follows a resumable page-job lifecycle (begin, submit_plan, next_page, submit_page, finish) with a durable ordered queue checkpointed in openwiki/.run.json; each page becomes durable before advancing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c50df9377a7b1a93d01457c261ada7523e340feb6608910be5495eeb8bc5e78f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per the README, host-driven coding-agent runs support only repository code wikis (not personal brains), use only repository source and tests (no connector context including LangSmith), and Grounded Claims apply only to repository evidence."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c64f28cea96f70a75e0a55daecc1e11a85f6bdf279b23ab30c563ec0e12c7450"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Output follows Open Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.2 with YAML front matter, generated/verified provenance stamps, validated optional trust and lifecycle fields, and reserved index.md and log.md documents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_edfaf9164c195d4dd57e3b71427056ea3c327f61c72787fe02e9b8f40534fa48"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI requires Node.js 22 or newer, installs via npm, and depends on the better-sqlite3 native module, which on Windows may need Visual Studio Build Tools if installed with bun."}],"claim_ids":["clm_148cfc859248fea87666537a7e52ff3d943e379730ff796e1e91d4e2d0ca04af","clm_23d70d663bfdbfde2118e42a646d7cf5074e77fae68ab7ba849e2986f108f797","clm_297282fa7f053d3a0a473513e571555c644e12b07fdcee8445db50113c17dd37","clm_2b778e362b789acf06c003e9b25f5e597765d6c63ab65aca0828a993832ae22f","clm_4192d1f20a41790de62927a8bf4e23e50a578911d424b6b5c161ae53da67143e","clm_458eb8c35b488e7bbd5daeb0ea605e97f9f53dbdf6a981e784eea8dd052280f2","clm_528cc5c643665c905dd3e157be0e367b6ab38dfc352531c99cbc5402e53ff779","clm_9433e3f7348319bb6dce728194df4e95348727219e5bf8067ffa98bf1cdf21cc","clm_a27e5781554a893e3a776cb10305633de0a19df1691c8c5eebb56741792b23e2","clm_c50df9377a7b1a93d01457c261ada7523e340feb6608910be5495eeb8bc5e78f","clm_c64f28cea96f70a75e0a55daecc1e11a85f6bdf279b23ab30c563ec0e12c7450","clm_edfaf9164c195d4dd57e3b71427056ea3c327f61c72787fe02e9b8f40534fa48"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:40Z","created_by_operation":"op_df82d93b9d78477fb22075a6516db635","id":"pg_5de9ca7f201854a78bcbbf149664f367","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langchain-ai-openwiki-readme-md-e92cc11723a8-bf149664f367.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3bd011bc315c56aaaa558de8bd0d9c1b"],"title":"langchain-ai/openwiki/README.md @ e92cc11723a8","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:40Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df82d93b9d78477fb22075a6516db635"}
